{"sourceSha256": "f1b9bb9a02efc4173f8b164237caa0db996fd047d49265ae604a0040d5489ebd", "text": "Ticket Id: 26905\n\nDr Jose Jiminez\nSurgeon\nMelbourne Private Hospital\n19 Grange Road\nMelbourne 3000\n\n22/01/2007\n\nRE: Mrs Ann Howard, DOB: 1971\n\nThank you for seeing Mrs Howard who presented with symptoms and signs suggestive of early stage of\nintestinal obstruction. Your further assessment would be appreciated.\n\nMrs Howard is a 36-year-old married woman. She has a past history of ovarian cystectomy,\nappendicectomy and spontanous abortion.                                                                        Commented [B1]: possible spontaneous\n\nOn 20/01/2007, she presented with a severe persistent lower abdominal pain. Her pain was more\nprominent on the left side. Moreover, sitting up, walking or bending exacerbated her pain. No associated\nsymptoms were reported apart from similar pain one day ago which was relieved by Valium. On                    Commented [B2]: a\nexamination, the left lower quadrant of the abdomen was tender. An abdominal mass was palpable also.\nThree days later, she reported mild improvement of the pain. However, there were no bowel movements\nover the last 3 days except one time of hard stool mixed with bright blood.                                    Commented [B3]: passing\n\nToday, she presented with a worsening pain following eating, associated with constipation and inability to     Commented [B4]: the\npass flatus. Examinations revealed a moderated tense abdomen as well as quit bowel sounds\n\nIn view of the above, my provisional diagnosis is early stage of intestinal obstruction. I suspect it may be\ndiverticulitis or carcinoma. I would appreciate your further evaluation and management as you see\nsuitable.\n\nFor any queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n\n                                     Report\n Word length                  211\n Comments                     Meets expectations.\