ing eating, associated with constipation and inability to     Commented [B4]: the\npass flatus. Examinations revealed a moderated tense abdomen as well as quit bowel sounds\n\nIn view of the above, my provisional diagnosis is early stage of intestinal obstruction. I suspect it may be\ndiverticulitis or carcinoma. I would appreciate your further evaluation and management as you see\nsuitable.\n\nFor any queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n\n                                     Report\n Word length                  211\n Comments                     Meets expectations.\n Estimated Grade              B+\n Advice                       1. Revise grammar.\n                              2. Be careful with spelling.\n                              3. Always proofread the letter after finishing it.\n Helpful links                https://www.benchmarkedu.com.au/oet-reading-\n                              practice-tests\n                              https://www.benchmarkedu.com.au/oet-writing-\n                              correction\n                              https://www.facebook.com/groups/oethelp\n\n\n\n\n296 Henley Beach Rd, Underdale, 5032\nhttp://www.benchmarkedu.com.au/oet-writing-correction\nwww.benchmarkedu.com.au/pteoetielts", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "Ticket Id: 26905\n\nDr Jose Jiminez\nSurgeon\nMelbourne Private Hospital\n19 Grange Road\nMelbourne 3000\n\n22/01/2007\n\nRE: Mrs Ann Howard, DOB: 1971\n\nThank you for seeing Mrs Howard who presented with symptoms and signs suggestive of early stage of\nintestinal obstruction. Your further assessment would be appreciated.\n\nMrs Howard is a 36-year-old married woman. She has a past history of ovarian cystectomy,\nappendicectomy and spontanous abortion.\n\nOn 20/01/2007, she presented with a severe persistent lower abdominal pain. Her pain was more\nprominent on the left side. Moreover, sitting up, walking or bending exacerbated her pain. No 